\fs64 \cf2 Example: Copying data\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 This example shows how reflected field information can drive real behavior. It uses reflection to copy data from one instance to another by iterating over fields and checking which ones are safe to copy. This pattern demonstrates how reflection enables generic, type-safe operations without hardcoding field access.\
When a struct conforms to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 MakeCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , it gains the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 copy_to()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  method that uses reflection to perform the copy. Like all methods, you call it from an instance. For this method, you provide it with a target instance.\
Its behavior is similar in spirit to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 ImplicitlyCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , but 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 copy_to()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  limits copying to fields whose types conform to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 Copyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . It requires an already initialized target, avoiding matching values to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 __init__
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  arguments.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 from\cf16  std\cf5 .\cf16 reflection \cf5 import\cf16  struct_field_count\cf5 ,\cf16  struct_field_types\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 trait\cf16  MakeCopyable\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  \cf18 copy_to\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf5 mut\cf16  other\cf5 :\cf16  Self\cf5 ):\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 comptime\cf16  field_count \cf5 =\cf16  struct_field_count\cf5 [\cf16 Self\cf5 ]()\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 comptime\cf16  field_types \cf5 =\cf16  struct_field_types\cf5 [\cf16 Self\cf5 ]()\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15         \cf5 comptime\cf16  \cf5 for\cf16  idx \cf5 in\cf16  \cf18 range\cf5 (\cf16 field_count\cf5 ):\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15             \cf5 comptime\cf16  field_type \cf5 =\cf16  field_types\cf5 [\cf16 idx\cf5 ]\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15             \cf6 # Guard: field type must be copyable\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15             \cf5 comptime\cf16  \cf5 if\cf16  \cf5 not\cf16  conforms_to\cf5 (\cf16 field_type\cf5 ,\cf16  Copyable\cf5 ):\cf16  \cf5 continue\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15             \cf6 # Perform the copy\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15             \cf5 ref\cf16  p_value \cf5 =\cf16  __struct_field_ref\cf5 (\cf16 idx\cf5 ,\cf16  self\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15             trait_downcast\cf5 [\cf16 Copyable \cf5 &\cf16  ImplicitlyDestructible\cf5 ](\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15                 __struct_field_ref\cf5 (\cf16 idx\cf5 ,\cf16  other\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15             \cf5 )\cf16  \cf5 =\cf16  trait_downcast\cf5 [\cf16 Copyable \cf5 &\cf16  ImplicitlyDestructible\cf5 ](\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15                 p_value\cb1 \
\cb15             \cf5 ).\cf16 copy\cf5 ()\cf16 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

