\fs48 \cf2 Insights\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The function iterates over reflected fields and checks each one for 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 Copyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  conformance, skipping any field that cannot be copied.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
As a method, 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 copy_to()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  does not require a type parameter such as 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 copy_to[T]()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . It has direct access to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 Self
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , which is enabled by 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 MakeCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  trait adoption.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 copy_to()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  implementation is heavily parameterized and evaluated at compile time. It uses 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 comptime for
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 comptime if
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  together with reflection calls.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 __struct_field_ref(idx, self)
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 __struct_field_ref(idx, other)
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  calls return references to fields by index, which allows both reading from the source instance and writing to the destination instance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Create a struct\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The following 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 MultiType
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  struct conforms to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 MakeCopyable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  meaning you can call 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 copy_to
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  on its instances:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 @fieldwise_init\cf16 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb15 struct\cf16  \cf18 MultiType\cf5 (\cf16 Writable\cf5 ,\cf16  MakeCopyable\cf5 ):\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf16  w\cf5 :\cf16  String\cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf16  x\cf5 :\cf16  Int\cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf16  y\cf5 :\cf16  Bool\cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf16  z\cf5 :\cf16  Float64\cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 def\cf16  write_to\cf5 [\cf16 W\cf5 :\cf16  Writer\cf5 ](\cf16 self\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf5 mut\cf16  writer\cf5 :\cf16  W\cf5 ):\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         writer\cf5 .\cf16 write\cf5 (\cf17 "[\{\}, \{\}, \{\}, \{\}]"\cf5 .\cf18 format\cf5 (\cf16 self\cf5 .\cf16 w\cf5 ,\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 x\cf5 ,\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 y\cf5 ,\cf16  self\cf5 .\cf16 z\cf5 ))\cf16 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

