\fs64 \cf2 Example: Testing equality\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 This example demonstrates how reflection can be used to implement structural equality. Compile-time loop unrolling, conformance checks, and reflection drive runtime comparisons. This is the same pattern used for generic equality, hashing, and validation logic.\
In each iteration, 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 test_equality
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  checks for 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 Equatable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  conformance and retrieves field value references from the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 lhs
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 rhs
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  arguments. It uses early return for the first inequality (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 False
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ), otherwise returning 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 :\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 from\cf16  std\cf5 .\cf16 reflection \cf5 import\cf16  struct_field_count\cf5 ,\cf16  struct_field_types\cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb15 def\cf16  test_equality\cf5 [\cf16 T\cf5 :\cf16  AnyType\cf5 ](\cf16 lhs\cf5 :\cf16  T\cf5 ,\cf16  rhs\cf5 :\cf16  T\cf5 )\cf16  \cf5 ->\cf16  Bool\cf5 :\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 comptime\cf16  field_count \cf5 =\cf16  struct_field_count\cf5 [\cf16 T\cf5 ]()\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 comptime\cf16  field_types \cf5 =\cf16  struct_field_types\cf5 [\cf16 T\cf5 ]()\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 comptime\cf16  \cf5 for\cf16  idx \cf5 in\cf16  \cf18 range\cf5 (\cf16 field_count\cf5 ):\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf6 # Guard: field type must be equatable\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 comptime\cf16  field_type \cf5 =\cf16  field_types\cf5 [\cf16 idx\cf5 ]\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 comptime\cf16  \cf5 if\cf16  \cf5 not\cf16  conforms_to\cf5 (\cf16 field_type\cf5 ,\cf16  Equatable\cf5 ):\cf16  \cf5 continue\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15         \cf6 # Fetch values\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 ref\cf16  lhs_value \cf5 =\cf16  __struct_field_ref\cf5 (\cf16 idx\cf5 ,\cf16  lhs\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 ref\cf16  rhs_value \cf5 =\cf16  __struct_field_ref\cf5 (\cf16 idx\cf5 ,\cf16  rhs\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15         \cf6 # Early exit with `False` when inequality found\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 if\cf16  trait_downcast\cf5 [\cf16 Equatable\cf5 ](\cf16 lhs_value\cf5 )\cf16  \cf5 !=\cf16  trait_downcast\cf5 [\cf16 Equatable\cf5 ](\cf16 rhs_value\cf5 ):\cf16  \cf5 return\cf16  \cf19 False\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\cb15     \cf5 return\cf16  \cf19 True\cf16 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

