\fs48 \cf2 Insights\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
This example uses two key elements to ensure smooth operation: 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 conforms_to()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 trait_downcast[]()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
conforms_to()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  ensures each field's type is 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 Equatable
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and therefore works with the inequality operator (
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 !=
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 ).\
\ls7\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
trait_downcast
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is used with parameter input types. It rebinds a typed value, returning a value that conforms to the specified 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 Trait
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . If its type, after resolution, does not conform to that trait, it will produce a compilation error. Checking for conformance first ensures that error won't occur.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
As its name suggests, 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 __struct_field_ref()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is limited to use with struct types.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Calling the tests\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 To demonstrate this function, the following 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 main()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  first copies values (equal), and then mutates 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb14 original_instance
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  and tests again (unequal):\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb15 def\cf16  \cf18 main\cf5 ():\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf16  original_instance \cf5 =\cf16  MultiType\cf5 (\cf17 "Hello"\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf19 1\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf19 True\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf19 2.5\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 var\cf16  target_instance \cf5 =\cf16  MultiType\cf5 (\cf17 ""\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf19 0\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf19 False\cf5 ,\cf16  \cf19 0.0\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     original_instance\cf5 .\cf16 copy_to\cf5 (\cf16 target_instance\cf5 )\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 print(\cf17 "Values equal"\cf16  \cf5 if\cf16  \\\cb1 \
\cb15         test_equality\cf5 (\cf16 original_instance\cf5 ,\cf16  target_instance\cf5 )\cf16  \\\cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 else\cf16  \cf17 "Values not equal"\cf5 )\cf16  \cf6 # Values equal\cf16 \cb1 \
\
\
\cb15     original_instance\cf5 .\cf16 z \cf5 =\cf16  \cf19 42.0\cf16 \cb1 \
\cb15     \cf5 print(\cf17 "Values equal"\cf16  \cf5 if\cf16  \\\cb1 \
\cb15         test_equality\cf5 (\cf16 original_instance\cf5 ,\cf16  target_instance\cf5 )\cf16  \\\cb1 \
\cb15         \cf5 else\cf16  \cf17 "Values not equal"\cf5 )\cf16  \cf6 # Values not equal\cf16 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

